3. Binary Search Logic

Initialize start = 0 and end = n - 1.

Calculate the middle index:

mid = start + (end - start) / 2;

Calculate the missing count:

arr[mid] - mid - 1

If the missing count is greater than or equal to k:

Store mid in ans.

Search the left half using end = mid - 1.

Otherwise:

Search the right half using start = mid + 1.

Initialize ans = n so that the code also works when the answer lies beyond the last array element.

Return:

ans + k
